{% from "icon/macro.njk" import icon %}

{# The one thing on these pages that needs a line of script, and it earns it:
   an operator's whole job here is to carry an id or a reference somewhere else
   — into a log query, into a ticket, into Slack — and selecting eight
   characters of mono out of a dense row with a mouse is a fiddle they were
   doing twenty times an hour.

   Progressive by construction. The button ships `disabled`, because a button
   that looks live and does nothing when clicked is worse than no button: with
   scripting off, or before the module has run, it is visibly inert rather
   than a broken promise. `do-copy-button` enables it on upgrade, and only when
   the clipboard API is actually there to enable it for.

   Stock daisyUI: a square ghost button in a `tooltip`, which is what says what
   the icon is for without a word of layout. It is drawn at all times — this
   page has a handful of them, each beside a value the operator came here to
   carry somewhere else, and a button they have to find by hovering is a button
   they do not know is there. The list, which would have had forty, has none:
   every id there is one click from the page that draws it whole.

   The label carries the noun — `Copy event id` — because "Copy" alone names
   nothing for a screen reader walking the row.

   Both glyphs are in the markup and daisyUI's `swap` shows one of them: the
   check has to replace the copy glyph for a second and a half without the
   button changing size, and a swap the element did by rewriting innerHTML
   would throw the row's layout for a frame. #}
<do-copy-button class="inline-flex shrink-0 align-middle" value="{{ params.value }}" data-testid="do-copy-button">
  <div class="tooltip" data-tip="Copy {{ params.what }}">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-xs btn-square" aria-label="Copy {{ params.what }}" disabled data-testid="do-copy-button-control">
      <span class="swap" data-testid="do-copy-button-swap">
        {{ icon({ name: 'copy', class: 'swap-off size-3.5 opacity-60' }) }}
        {{ icon({ name: 'check', class: 'swap-on size-3.5 text-success' }) }}
      </span>
    </button>
  </div>
</do-copy-button>
